From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 07:28:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07053/11362] [outer-loop] Task 9: exp5701 broader-headroom
 re-run of task-12 candidate-scoring ablation

Re-scopes exp5592's candidate-scoring-stack vs bare-control ablation
(REQ-ARC-FCP-5592) after diagnosing its result as a floor-effect artifact:
only 1 of 11 games (lp85) showed any level progress in either arm, and that
game tied identically -- not a genuine measurement of whether the stack
earns its keep.

Root cause (same-session calibration probe): exp5592's roster mixed
adaptered and un-adaptered games (wa30, sc25 have no registered GameAdapter
and scored 0 at budget=200 AND budget=600 -- structurally unreachable, not
signal). Raising budget 200->600 on adaptered games lifted the level>=1 hit
rate from ~9% to ~50%.

exp5701 re-runs the IDENTICAL ablation methodology (same BARE_CONTROL_KWARGS,
same CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_INDUCTION=1 isolation) on the full 22-game
arc_game_adapters.adaptered_games() roster at budget=500. Real result
(duration_s=1255.5): n_games_with_headroom=5 (lp85, sp80, su15, tu93, vc33,
up from 1) -- full stack won tu93 (+1 level), bare control won sp80 (+1
level), three-way tie elsewhere; total levels tied 4-4 but efficiency
favored the full stack 4.5384 vs 2.862 (mainly vc33: same level, ~45x more
efficient). Adversarially clean.

Adds python/carnot/experiment_5701_candidate_scoring_stack_bare_control_ab_headroom.py
+ its real result artifact + 7 tests (blocked-precondition, headroom-count
reporting, no-headroom honest-null, and a real-artifact assertion test) +
REQ-ARC-FCP-5701-HEADROOM-RESCOPE spec.md section + ops/known-issues.md
task-12 closure note.

